<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU tweaks textiles imports system.</title>
<headline>EU tweaks textiles imports system.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The General Affairs Council agreed on Tuesday to amend the EU's common system of textiles imports quotas for third countries.</p>
<p>The amendments were drawn up in response to concerns that some countries were overshooting the EU's quotas for items like underwear and that the EU could not do anything about it as rules stood.</p>
<p>Under the amended rules the countries concerned can continue to overshoot quotas, but only on the condition that they inform the EU and that the overshoot is compensated for elsewhere -- for example in a quota for another product, or the quota for the same product the year after.</p>
</text>
